From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0091] anv: clear the whole sampler state before packing it

On top of 0090 (src/mesa-cts1, build-cts1). NOT installed.

genX(emit_sampler_state) packs SAMPLER_STATE (4 dwords on Gfx12/Xe2) into slots of ANV_SAMPLER_STATE_DWORDS (8)
and never wrote the other 4. anv_WriteSamplerDescriptorsEXT (VK_EXT_descriptor_heap) packs into an
uninitialized stack struct anv_sampler_state and copies ANV_SAMPLER_STATE_SIZE (32) bytes, the reported sampler
descriptor size, so the upper 16 bytes of every sampler descriptor were stack garbage.
dEQP-VK.binding_model.descriptor_heap.capture_replay.sampler{,_custom_border} compare two writes of the same
sampler made from different call histories: "Descriptor data is not invariant" (2 fails; the invariance.*
variant passes only because its writes come from one tight loop with identical stack contents).
anv_nir_lower_descriptor_heap had the same garbage in embedded_key.sampler, which is hashed and compared for
embedded samplers. vkCreateSampler was not affected (its state is in zeroed object memory).

Generated-by: LLM

diff --git a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_init_state.c b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_init_state.c
index c849fcf..f2e8e61 100644
--- a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_init_state.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_init_state.c
@@ -1464,6 +1464,15 @@ genX(emit_sampler_state)(const struct anv_device *device,
    const bool seamless_cube =
       !(vk_state->flags & VK_SAMPLER_CREATE_NON_SEAMLESS_CUBE_MAP_BIT_EXT);
 
+   /* SAMPLER_STATE is 4 dwords but each plane slot is
+    * ANV_SAMPLER_STATE_DWORDS (8) dwords, all of which are copied out: into
+    * descriptor heaps by vkWriteSamplerDescriptorsEXT (descriptor size
+    * ANV_SAMPLER_STATE_SIZE) and into embedded_key, which is hashed and
+    * compared. The callers may pass uninitialized stack memory, so clear the
+    * whole state for the unused dwords to be zero instead of stack garbage.
+    */
+   memset(state, 0, sizeof(*state));
+
    const struct vk_format_ycbcr_info *ycbcr_info =
       vk_state->has_ycbcr_conversion ?
       vk_format_get_ycbcr_info(vk_state->format) : NULL;
